<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Entering the Dancepalooza</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;The universe is in crisis and only a dance competition can save it! At least, that's what the writer told me to say. Why did they spend over a month on this silly fic and why did he divide it into two (possible) chapters? You can ask them that. I'm only here as an observer of the shenanigans. Anyway, enjoy yourselves, folks and this lovely romp on the planet ofâ€¦uhâ€¦who knows whereâ€¦it's a competition and it's in some auditoriumâ€¦it could be anywhereâ€¦but it's a fun ride for all involvedâ€¦including me, the disembodied narrator!&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>lefemmerouge</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Teen And Up Audiences</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Carmen Sandiego (Cartoon 2019)</rdf:li>
